**Included:** one process (vendor onboarding), synthetic data, English only, CLI run, one report.

**Excluded:** UI, real bank data, integrations, scheduling, multi-process runs, internet/news research.

**Success metrics**
- 100% of seeded "not applicable but loss event exists" cases are flagged.
- 0 cases of zero residual risk where a loss event exists.
- 100% of challenges cite an evidence ID.
- One full run under 2 minutes and under €0.10 in API cost.
- Reviewer agreement ≥ 80% on challenges.

## 4. Risk Assessment

| # | Risk | Category | Prob. | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | LLM proposes irrelevant or invented risks | Technical | Medium | High | Restrict proposals to the risk library taxonomy; validate output against library IDs; reject unknown IDs |
| 2 | LLM changes a challenge decision (hallucinated pass/fail) | Technical | Medium | High | Challenge rules and scoring in deterministic Python; LLM only writes the explanation |
| 3 | Malformed LLM JSON breaks the graph | Technical | Medium | Medium | Structured output / Pydantic schema; one retry; fail the node with a clear error |
| 4 | API cost or rate limits | Technical | Low | Medium | gpt-4o-mini; one call per step, not per risk; log token usage per run |
| 5 | Loss events not tagged to process step | Data | High | High | Mapping table step → risk category; flag untagged events as "unmapped" in report instead of ignoring them |
| 6 | Confidential loss data sent to external LLM | Data / privacy | Medium | High | Synthetic data in MVP; in production, send only IDs and categories, no amounts or names; enterprise API / data processing agreement |
| 7 | Owners see the tool as a "policing" tool and resist | Business | Medium | Medium | Position as preparation support; owner sees challenges before second line |
| 8 | Scope creep into a full GRC tool | Business | High | Medium | Fixed MVP list above; new requests go to v2 backlog |
| 9 | Over-reliance: second line accepts AI output without review | Business / governance | Medium | High | Mandatory human validation node; report marked "draft" until approved |

## 5. Implementation Plan

| Phase | Work | Estimate | Milestone |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Setup and data | Synthetic vendor onboarding process, previous RCSA, risk library, loss events, KRIs (JSON/CSV); state schema | 1 day | Data files load and validate |
| 2. Core agent | LangGraph nodes: load → propose risks → collect answers → challenge → score → report; tools | 2 days | One run end to end |
| 3. Integration and testing | Seeded test cases, rule unit tests, error handling, trace logging | 1 day | All success metrics pass on test set |
| 4. Deployment and monitoring | README, run script, cost/token logging, human validation step | 1 day | Reviewer can reproduce one run |

**Dependencies:** OpenAI API key; synthetic data must exist before Phase 2; risk library must be fixed before rule tests.

**Resources**
- Team: me (developer + risk SME); one reviewer from the cohort/instructor for agreement check.
- Tools: Python, LangGraph, OpenAI API, VS Code, GitHub.
- Budget: MVP API cost below €5 for all development and test runs (gpt-4o-mini).

## 6. Success Metrics

**MVP (technical):** seeded-issue detection rate 100%, evidence citation rate 100%, run time < 2 min, cost per run < €0.10.

**Business (after pilot):**
- Time to complete one process RCSA reduced from weeks of workshops to one owner session plus one review.
- Share of owner answers changed after challenge (shows the challenge adds value).
- Number of "not applicable" answers overturned by evidence.
